            "url": "https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/pull/511339",
            "title": "lomiri.lomiri-polkit-agent: 0.3.2 -> 0.3.3",
            "date_modified": "2026-04-19T10:23:27.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-04-19T10:08:30.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "OPNA2608",
                "url": "https://github.com/OPNA2608"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/141248?u=6a66083b268f747fb195b446d42cb0b29346abf9&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Generalises the existing <code class=\"notranslate\">--sudo</code> handling into a small <code class=\"notranslate\">Elevator</code> abstraction and adds a <code class=\"notranslate\">run0</code> backend, so activation commands on the local machine or a <code class=\"notranslate\">--target-host</code> can be elevated via systemd's polkit-based <code class=\"notranslate\">run0</code> instead of <code class=\"notranslate\">sudo</code>.<br>\nMore backends could be added in the future without major rework.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">--elevate {none,sudo,run0}</code> selects the backend; <code class=\"notranslate\">--ask-elevate-password</code> (<code class=\"notranslate\">-S</code>) prompts locally and feeds the password to it. <code class=\"notranslate\">--sudo</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">--use-remote-sudo</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">--ask-sudo-password</code> are kept as deprecated aliases.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">For the local case, we run <code class=\"notranslate\">run0 -- &lt;cmd&gt;</code> and the user's normal polkit agent (graphical or <code class=\"notranslate\">pkttyagent</code>) handles any prompt.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">For the remote case there is no controlling terminal over the SSH pipe, so the non-interactive <code class=\"notranslate\">systemd-run --uid=0 --pipe --wait ...</code> form is used.<br>\nA transient unit does not inherit the SSH login environment, on NixOS its <code class=\"notranslate\">PATH</code> is just the systemd store path, so the env-resolution shell wrapper runs in the login shell <em>around</em> <code class=\"notranslate\">systemd-run</code> and forwards the resolved values into the unit via <code class=\"notranslate\">--setenv</code>.<br>\nTo express that, <code class=\"notranslate\">Elevator.wrap_remote()</code> takes the env mapping and command and returns the full remote argv (sudo keeps the env wrapper inside itself, run0 puts it around).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Without <code class=\"notranslate\">--ask-elevate-password</code> this relies on a polkit rule on the target granting the deploying user <code class=\"notranslate\">org.freedesktop.systemd1.manage-units</code> (e.g. via <code class=\"notranslate\">security.polkit.extraConfig</code>).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">With <code class=\"notranslate\">--ask-elevate-password</code> the remote command is wrapped in <code class=\"notranslate\">polkit-stdin-agent</code> (new package), which registers a per-process polkit agent for the <code class=\"notranslate\">systemd-run</code> child and answers the PAM conversation from stdin (there is no direct <code class=\"notranslate\">sudo --stdin</code> equivalent for polkit).<br>\nThe agent binary is referenced by store path so it is reachable on the target via the <code class=\"notranslate\">nixos-rebuild</code> closure once that system has been deployed once with this PR included.<br>\nThe first deploy will need a final <code class=\"notranslate\">--elevate=sudo</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I added a subtest to <code class=\"notranslate\">nixosTests.nixos-rebuild-target-host</code> that tests the full <code class=\"notranslate\">--elevate=run0 --ask-elevate-password</code> path end-to-end.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Supersedes <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4208494824\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/issues/507054\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/NixOS/nixpkgs/pull/507054/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/pull/507054\">#507054</a>.<br>\nCC: <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/Jappie3/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/Jappie3\">@Jappie3</a></p>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Things done</h2>\n\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li>Built on platform:\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> x86_64-linux</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> aarch64-linux</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> x86_64-darwin</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> aarch64-darwin</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Tested, as applicable:\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> <a href=\"https://nixos.org/manual/nixos/unstable/index.html#sec-nixos-tests\" rel=\"nofollow\">NixOS tests</a> in <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/nixos/tests\">nixos/tests</a>.</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/pkgs/README.md#package-tests\">Package tests</a> at <code class=\"notranslate\">passthru.tests</code>.</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Tests in <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/lib/tests\">lib/tests</a> or <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/pkgs/test\">pkgs/test</a> for functions and \"core\" functionality.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Ran <code class=\"notranslate\">nixpkgs-review</code> on this PR. See <a href=\"https://github.com/Mic92/nixpkgs-review#usage\">nixpkgs-review usage</a>.</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> Tested basic functionality of all binary files, usually in <code class=\"notranslate\">./result/bin/</code>.</li>\n<li>Nixpkgs Release Notes\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Package update: when the change is major or breaking.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>NixOS Release Notes\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Module addition: when adding a new NixOS module.</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Module update: when the change is significant.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> Fits <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md\">CONTRIBUTING.md</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/pkgs/README.md\">pkgs/README.md</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/maintainers/README.md\">maintainers/README.md</a> and other READMEs.</li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/pull/512018",
            "title": "nixos-rebuild-ng: add --elevate={sudo,run0} and polkit-stdin-agent",
            "date_modified": "2026-04-21T20:59:10.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-04-21T08:19:00.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "r-vdp",
                "url": "https://github.com/r-vdp"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14929991?u=bbf4ea0fb9459a159074011ad21d21a66f3ac269&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR introduces a <code class=\"notranslate\">security.polkit.packages</code> option. We have this types of option for dbus and systemd already, but for polkit you had to add the packages to <code class=\"notranslate\">environment.systemPackages</code> with the side effect of cluttering up <code class=\"notranslate\">bin</code> and other directories.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I have migrated some modules that contained a comment stating polkit was the only reason for including a package in <code class=\"notranslate\">systemPackages</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is a breaking change that will affect some people, I have added a release note about this. <a href=\"https://github.com/search?q=lang%3Anix+-is%3Afork+%22environment.etc.%5C%22polkit-1%22&amp;type=code\">A GitHub search shows about 50 cases</a>, although some of those are likely manual forks and nixpkgs modules.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">There isn't any test for polkit at the moment, but the rtkit test depends heavily on polkit, so I've used this to verify that the changes look okay.</p>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Things done</h2>\n\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li>Built on platform:\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> x86_64-linux</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> aarch64-linux</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> x86_64-darwin</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> aarch64-darwin</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Tested, as applicable:\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> <a href=\"https://nixos.org/manual/nixos/unstable/index.html#sec-nixos-tests\" rel=\"nofollow\">NixOS tests</a> in <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/nixos/tests\">nixos/tests</a>.</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/pkgs/README.md#package-tests\">Package tests</a> at <code class=\"notranslate\">passthru.tests</code>.</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Tests in <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/lib/tests\">lib/tests</a> or <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/pkgs/test\">pkgs/test</a> for functions and \"core\" functionality.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> Ran <code class=\"notranslate\">nixpkgs-review</code> on this PR. See <a href=\"https://github.com/Mic92/nixpkgs-review#usage\">nixpkgs-review usage</a>.</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Tested basic functionality of all binary files, usually in <code class=\"notranslate\">./result/bin/</code>.</li>\n<li>Nixpkgs Release Notes\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Package update: when the change is major or breaking.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>NixOS Release Notes\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Module addition: when adding a new NixOS module.</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> Module update: when the change is significant.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> Fits <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md\">CONTRIBUTING.md</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/pkgs/README.md\">pkgs/README.md</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/maintainers/README.md\">maintainers/README.md</a> and other READMEs.</li>\n</ul>",
